# How to fill these:
# 1. tenantAId / tenantBId / resourceAId: run against the live DB —
#      select id, name from tenants;
#      select id, name from resources;
#    tenantAId = the tenant with owner/staff/viewer members (e.g. "Demo
#    Tenant"), tenantBId = any other tenant the same users are NOT
#    members of (e.g. "Second Studio"). resourceAId = a resource that
#    belongs to tenantAId.
# 2. ownerAEmail/ownerAPassword, staffAEmail/staffAPassword,
#    viewerAEmail/viewerAPassword: the real demo accounts created via
#    the web sign-up flow (owner/staff/viewer members of tenantAId).
#    Fill these in Bruno's environment editor directly — never commit
#    real passwords into this file.
# 3. Run the three requests in bruno/setup/ (sign-in-owner, sign-in-staff,
#    sign-in-viewer) once — each one signs in against Supabase Auth
#    directly and writes the resulting access_token into ownerAToken /
#    staffAToken / viewerAToken automatically via a post-response script.
#    No manual copy-pasting of JWTs required.
